  "text": "# What `serve/server.py` does\n\n`serve/server.py` is the HTTP front door of Strata: it is the process that listens on port 8080 and turns OpenAI Chat Completions and Anthropic Messages requests into token-id prompts for the C++ engine, then streams the engine's token output back as text deltas. Its main pieces are:\n\n- **Engine adapters.** `Engine` is a protocol (`generate(ids, max_new, sampling, cancel) -> iterator of token ids`). `MockEngine` replays a scripted completion for tests without a GPU. `StrataEngine` keeps one `strata --serve` process resident (weights, expert arena and VRAM tier load once), talks to it over stdin/stdout with `GEN <max_new> [sampling keys] <ids>` lines, and reads back `T <id>` token lines, `PP` prompt-progress lines, `INFO` facts, and a `DONE` line whose fields it parses in `_parse_done` (generated/prompt tokens, prompt/decode ms, finish reason, drafts, hit rate, and the expert-tier counters added in 0.1.31). It narrates startup from the engine log (`narrate_start`),",
